cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use v2vtrack, please cite it as below."
title: "v2vtrack: online array-offset tracking for position-aided vehicle-to-vehicle beam prediction"
abstract: >-
  The position-aided beam map for a vehicle-to-vehicle millimetre-wave link fails across recordings because the
  receiver's array offset relative to its GPS-derived heading differs by a few degrees between recordings and
  drifts within one, and because the heading is unobservable at low speed. v2vtrack implements the offset
  analysis on DeepSense 6G scenarios 36-39, a one-state Kalman tracker fed by sparse beam sweeps or a local
  sweep that restores the map online without labels, the static-map, beam-hold, offset-tracking, windowed-refit
  and learned baselines with test-time adaptation and supervised fine-tuning, a continual multi-scenario
  stream, and a known-truth validation on DeepMIMO v4 in which an applied array rotation is recovered below
  the beam width.
type: software
